{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>Or a root.</b> Like שרש (root). The meaning is that he reverted to Israelite practice, and he is of a ger's family and has no kin except himself. It is like the word ושרשך (Isaiah 53:2), opposite [of being uprooted]; likewise ואת סוסיהם תעקד (2 Kings 9:25)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Resolved the two biblical allusions by verse reference. The phrase 'reverted to Israelite practice' renders ששב לדת ישראל literally; 'no kin except himself' renders אין ריע לו רק הוא."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:32.032943653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}